* How should inventory vs items be tracked?

### Option 1 - Itemid is the "class"

* ie it is the actual design and has a max quanitty and num sold attributes
* Seller (or Purchases/Refunds) can change the former and latter attributes respectively (transactions aside).
* Inventory table keeps track of user's "instance" anyway along with Txn ID (and price paid if different from listing price)
* Concurrency concerns

### Option2 - Each ItemId is a unique SKU

* Instead of maintaining a quantity field - just create X instances of the item.
* Downside is huge write traffic on each item creation.
* For UGC sites this could be expensive as with users
* Given 30M unique items - even with 1000 per item - would need 30B instances

So Pick option 1 for now and have an upgrade path to Option2 later (for uniqueness and trading)
Given UGC model - it is simpler (many users buying same limited/standard item)
